If you have some spare rings, there are two different rings that will
allow you to control the transformations, along with one amulet.

\SPOILER
Here's how to identify the rings and amulet:
1. Ring of protection from shape changers (cost 100) You'll be able to
see mimics in shops (if you have telepathy, remove its source to test
this).
If you have contracted lycanthropy, you will not change form.
Lycanthropes and other shape changers will be forced into their
natural forms.

USES: It can be a lifesaver on the rogue quest due to the plethora of
chameleons, some of which mimic dangerous creatures such as lichs
(touch of death, anyone?) and is valuable to early characters without
high magic cancellation (a property of certain cloaks and mithril that
reduces likelihood of "special" attacks such as poison bites or a
cockatrice's hissing harming you).

2. Amulet of unchanging. You will not mimic a pile of gold after
consuming a mimic, and will feel "momentarily different" after
stepping on a polytrap. You cannot turn into green slime (not too
helpful in the early game), but *can* be petrified. Zap a wand of
enlightenment while wearing it, if you possess one.

3. Ring of polymorph control. Allows you to control transformations
from human to wererat; you'll be prompted for whether you wish to
transform. Most expensive of the rings at 300, tied with teleport
control, conflict and polymorph. The best way to find it, since shape-
changing is often dangerous, is to prioritize identification of your
most expensive rings. Like any ring, zapping a wand of enlightenment
or dropping spares down a sink will identify the ring.

\END SPOILER



